<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch state raises tap price of 2007 bond to 99.40.</title>
<headline>Dutch state raises tap price of 2007 bond to 99.40.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finance Ministry raised the price for tap sales of the Dutch government's 5.75 percent bond due February 2007 to 99.40 from 99.35 early on Thursday.</p>
<p>Tap sales opened on Tuesday and had raised 3.2 billion guilders by the close of trade on Wednesday. They will continue daily from 0700 GMT until further notice.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
